---
// Verbatim Authentic Content & Media from Khao Sok Riverside Cottages
import PageLayout from '../../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';

---

<PageLayout
  title="Khao Sok National Park"
  description="Khao Sok National Park Discover more with our Khao Sok FAQs"
  heroImage="/images/khao-sok-hero-cottages.jpg"
  heroTitle="Khao Sok National Park"
  heroSubtitle="The Ancient Rainforest of Southern Thailand"
  breadcrumbs={[{"label": "Faq Category", "href": "/faq-category/"}, {"label": "Khao Sok National Park", "href": "/faq-category/khao-sok-national-park/"}]}
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-10">
    <div class="bg-[#faf8f5]/95 border border-[#12281b]/10 rounded-3xl p-4 sm:p-8 md:p-12 shadow-2xl backdrop-blur-md">
      
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-[#12281b]/10 pb-4 mb-8 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.22em] uppercase text-[#163824]">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 font-semibold">
          <span class="text-[#7a5813]">KSR</span>
          <span class="text-[#12281b]/20">/</span>
          <span>FIELD DISPATCH</span>
        </div>
        <span class="text-[#7a5813] font-bold">KHAO SOK · THAILAND</span>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-6 text-[#223e2c] text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed font-normal">

        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Is Khao Sok National Park worth visiting?</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Yes! There's always something exciting to discover in Khao Sok. Take in the views of stunning limestone cliffs, cruise around emerald Cheow Larn Lake, and spot thrilling local wildlife like monkeys, lizards, snakes, and even elephants. Cheow Larn Lake Trekking & Hiking
        </p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>When is the best time to visit Khao Sok National Park?</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          There are things to see and do in Khao Sok all year round. If you're looking for river tubing, that's best in June and September, the months with the most rainfall. The "green season" runs from May to October with alternating wet and dry weather. The weather is generally sunny and dry from November to April. Find out more..
        </p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>How do you get to Khao Sok National Park?</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          To get to Khao Sok national park you can take public transportation or hire a private transfer to get to Khao Sok. Transfers can be arranged from anywhere in southern Thailand. We have a detailed price list for transfers. Find transfers price list here.
        </p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Where is Khao Sok National Park?</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Khao Sok National Park is in Surat Thani in southwest Thailand. Its area is 739 km2 (285 sq mi), and it includes the 165 km2 (64 sq mi) Cheow Lan Lake Address: 62 Khlong Sok, Phanom District, Surat Thani 84250 The park gates are located at Khao Sok village. This page will help.
        </p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>What is Khao Sok National Park?</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Khao Sok National Park is known for being the world's oldest jungle ecosystem. This protected area of over 3,600 square kilometers is home to pristine jungle, waterfalls, swimming holes, and eye-catching limestone cliffs that rise sharply from the green canopy. Find out more ...
        </p>
      </div>

      
    </div>
  </article>
</PageLayout>
